Let's see if I have the third point right -

+ 1 added to the maximum arrows fired if you are an elf firing
elven arrows from an elven bow, an orc firing orcish arrows
from an orcish bow, a samurai firing ya from a regular bow, a
ranger firing racial arrows from a racial bow.

The first point is the to hit bonus which is important in the
early game but becomes irrelevant in the midgame once
luck is maxed out.

The second point is the damage bonus which is small but
real to the disadvantage of orcs compared to other archers.

The third the maximum number of arrows fired in a single
volley.  I suspect this factor overwhelms the other two - The
second biggest advantage of missile combat is multifire
ability to do enormous amounts of damage per volley.  The
first biggest advantage of missile combat is the target
monster can't hit you in melee and they generally come
with very few missiles.

Sounds to me like an orcish ranger doesn't have the
barrage advantage of other player character types but they
still have plentiful advantages against any game monster
when it comes to missile combat.  By the time luck and
strength and dexterity are maxed out and the arrows are
enchanted in the late game the difference becomes trivial
but it doesn't seem large to me even early on.


